xmodel/sol-symplectic.log:4631:dist/jc72108-theory-bundle-v1/xmodel/codex-eval-20260812.md:3050:SHEET6.md:20:- **The 4→5 explosion is NOT case count — it is a provable method failure.** Egorov 2002 constructed a proper 5-sheeted "exotic covering" of C² (branching along two planes F₁*,F₂*; H²_c ≅ Z²; S₁² = −3, S₂² = −15, S₁·S₂ = −3; K(S₁)=K(S₂)=1) consistent with EVERY quasi-topological invariant Domrina–Orevkov use. So 5 required a new analytic layer: both 2008 proofs inject Abhyankar approximate-root/Puiseux-coefficient arithmetic (pole orders of g along f-branches; jac=1 exponent identities) that sees strictly more than the topology. That is the conceptual jump; the case tree itself only grew ~2×.
