xmodel/sol-symplectic.log:6929:xmodel/sol-g5-emission.log:7005:   102	m = 2, b = (1,1): D5 forces both chains M=1/λ=0 single-orbit, μ = (1,1) at the meet. Interior meet: r = 2 in D6d, M = gcd(2, lν+1); M = 1 is killed at G\* by D3, so M = 2, i.e. lν odd: l odd ≥ 1 (l = 0 gives gcd(2ν, 2ν+1) = 1), ν odd. ν = 1: (iv) reduces to 2ps′ − l p′s = c′ ≠ 0 (ρ = 2/(2+l), L1 §4's reduction re-derived); l even: divide by p^{(l+2)/2} — (s·p^{−l/2})′ = (c′/2)p^{−(l+2)/2}, whose partial-fraction residue at each root is C(−n, n−1)(a₁−a₂)^{1−2n} with n = (l+2)/2 and C(−n,n−1) = (−1)^{n−1}·C(2n−2, n−1) ≠ 0 for ALL n ≥ 2 (exact; machine-verified n = 2..6) — a log term, so no rational s exists unless c′ = 0, contra ⊖ ≠ 0. This holds at ALL even l, td-uniformly (upgrading L1b beyond its engine caps). l odd gives M = gcd(2, 2+l) = 1, killed. Survivors: IIa(l odd, ν ≥ 3 odd) / ZCH(gcd(ν+1,l) ≥ 2) — exactly the L1 §3 blind-spot family, spend 0. Root meet: ν = 1 (St 9.2(ii)); l = 0: root law gives q = p and (iv) reads 0 = ⊖p ≠ 0 — impossible; l even: the same log-obstruction (u = 0 changes nothing); l odd: locally solvable at l = 1 (s = t − (a₁+a₂)/2, c′ = −(a₁−a₂)²/2, machine-verified exact), no M = 1 kill (Prop 8.3(iii) fails: two predecessors); printed pins: k_f = (2+l)l_f (D7 at r = 2), ψ = l+1 admissible, Σλ = 0 ⇒ l ≤ td−2 (St 9.4 (25)); [+H1] Prop 9.3(d) with child (ν,κ̄,D) = (1,1,l_f) gives 1 = (κ̄_i + n_i)/ν_i, n_i ≥ 1, so κ̄_i ≤ ν_i − 1 at both parents. td = 6: empty by reach (2POLE §5b phase 3). ∎
