xmodel/sol-symplectic.log:12504:SHEET6-MULTIPOLE.md-157-**The gap.** Everything printed now funnels into a single residual object: the **resonant jump vertex** — an all-M=1 merge with l ≥ 1 extra simple q-orbits, M = gcd(r, lν+1) ≥ 2 (or its ZCH/mixed analogues), spend 0, whose l extras no printed statement can see (Theorem O). For m = 2 this is exactly IIa(l odd, ν ≥ 3 odd, M = 2) / ZCH(gcd(ν+1,l) ≥ 2) at an interior meet, plus the root-meet l-odd residual; for m ≥ 3 the cells lν ≡ −1 (mod m) exist at pattern level but their *reachability* (r-edge ratio consistency) is untested. The kill, if one exists, must come from the H1 layer that the printed statements stop short of: matching the rigid (iv)-coefficients of a jump cell against the per-edge Prop 9.3(a)–(d) ratio equations of ALL r incoming chains simultaneously — a computation never yet run for any cell (the l = 1 rigidity a₁/a₂ = 2±√3 shows the coefficients are fully pinned, so the match is a finite check per cell).
