+## 5. Results
+
+This section is populated only from sealed, completed transcripts.
+
+## 6. Full-Cone Implication
+
+If `J_t^tail` has dimension zero, then every larger homogeneous ideal
+containing it also has dimension zero.  Therefore
+
+```text
+J_t^tail subset I_{t,+} and dim S_t/J_t^tail = 0
+  => dim S_t/I_{t,+} = 0.
+```
+
+Thus `(V0)` at `t=7` or `t=8` follows from the square-tail result alone.  The
+separate full-cone `t=7` computation is an additional run with the tail basis
+used as a starting basis, not the logical source of `(V0)`.
+
+## 7. Promotion Chain
+
+The properness gate promotes only the dimension-zero statement:
+
+```text
+modular dim=0  =>  characteristic-zero dim=0.
+```
+
+It does not promote modular Hilbert functions or modular lengths by flatness.
+For the square-tail test, once characteristic-zero dimension zero is promoted,
+Cohen-Macaulayness and the row degrees force the characteristic-zero complete-
+intersection Hilbert series separately.
+
+At each proved index, the promoted chain is:
